    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="instruction-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">MOVS (predicated)</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Move predicates (zeroing), setting the condition flags</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction reads Active elements from the source predicate and places those elements in the
corresponding elements of the destination predicate.
Inactive elements in the destination predicate register are set to zero. This instruction sets the First (N), None (Z), and !Last (C)
condition flags based on the predicate result,
and sets the V flag to zero.</p>
    <p>
        This is an alias of
        <a href="ands_p_p_pp.html">ANDS</a>.
        This means:
      </p><ul><li>
          The encodings in this description are named to match the encodings of
          <a href="ands_p_p_pp.html">ANDS</a>.
        </li><li>The description of <a href="ands_p_p_pp.html">ANDS</a> gives the operational pseudocode, any <span class="arm-defined-word">constrained unpredictable</span> behavior, and any operational information for this instruction.</li></ul>
    <h3 class="classheading"><a id="iclass_setting_the_condition_flags"></a>Setting the condition flags class
        <span style="font-size:smaller;"><br></br>(FEAT_SVE || FEAT_SME)
          </span></h3><p class="desc"></p><div class="regdiagram-32"><table class="regdiagram"><thead><tr><td>31</td><td>30</td><td>29</td><td>28</td><td>27</td><td>26</td><td>25</td><td>24</td><td>23</td><td>22</td><td>21</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>18</td><td>17</td><td>16</td><td>15</td><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>12</td><td>11</td><td>10</td><td>9</td><td>8</td><td>7</td><td>6</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="firstrow"><td class="l">0</td><td>0</td><td class="r">1</td><td class="l">0</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td class="r">0</td><td class="lr">1</td><td class="lr">0</td><td class="lr">1</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">0</td><td colspan="4" class="lr">Pm</td><td class="l">0</td><td class="r">1</td><td colspan="4" class="lr">Pg</td><td class="lr">0</td><td colspan="4" class="lr">Pn</td><td class="lr">0</td><td colspan="4" class="lr">Pd</td></tr><tr class="secondrow"><td colspan="3"></td><td colspan="4"></td><td></td><td class="droppedname">op</td><td class="droppedname">S</td><td colspan="2"></td><td colspan="4"></td><td colspan="2"></td><td colspan="4"></td><td class="droppedname">o2</td><td colspan="4"></td><td class="droppedname">o3</td><td colspan="4"></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="encoding"><div class="encoding__label"><h4 class="encoding">Encoding</h4><a id="movzs_p_p_p__ands_p_p_pp_z"></a></div><p class="asm-code">MOVS  <a href="#Pd" title='Is the name of the destination scalable predicate register, encoded in the "Pd" field.'>&lt;Pd&gt;</a>.B, <a href="#Pg__2" title='Is the name of the governing scalable predicate register, encoded in the "Pg" field.'>&lt;Pg&gt;</a>/Z, <a href="#Pn__3" title='Is the name of the source scalable predicate register, encoded in the "Pn" field.'>&lt;Pn&gt;</a>.B</p><p class="equivto">
      is equivalent to
    </p>
          <p class="asm-code"><a href="ands_p_p_pp.html#ands_p_p_pp_z">ANDS</a>  <a href="ands_p_p_pp.html#Pd">&lt;Pd&gt;</a>.B, <a href="ands_p_p_pp.html#Pg__2">&lt;Pg&gt;</a>/Z, <a href="ands_p_p_pp.html#Pn__2">&lt;Pn&gt;</a>.B, <a href="ands_p_p_pp.html#Pn__2">&lt;Pn&gt;</a>.B</p>
          <p class="equivto">
          and is the preferred disassembly when
          <span class="pseudocode">S == '1' &amp;&amp; Pn == Pm</span>.
        </p>
        </div>
